UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 3, Lesson 3: Place value problem solving', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Place-value problem solving uses digit values and regrouping to answer real questions about quantity, not digit tricks alone.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nThere are 3,060 stickers in packs of 10. How many packs? Show place reasoning.\n\nFEEDBACK\n306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens.\n\nWATCH FOR\nDividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nSolve four place-value word problems with new numbers (boxes of 10 and 100, leftover ones, comparing collections). Show working and a one-sentence reason for each.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Place-value problem solving uses digit values and regrouping to answer real questions about quantity, not digit tricks alone.","lesson_number":3,"lesson_role":"Problem solving","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-RN-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Solve four place-value word problems with new numbers (boxes of 10 and 100, leftover ones, comparing collections). Show working and a one-sentence reason for each. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original demonstration: A school has 2,450 pencils. A box holds 100. How many full boxes? 24 full boxes with 50 left over, because 24 hundreds make 2,400.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts. Correction: 306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts. Keep sample answers out of the child role.","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Place-value problem solving uses digit values and regrouping to answer real questions about quantity, not digit tricks alone. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Place-value problem solving uses digit values and regrouping to answer real questions about quantity, not digit tricks alone.","Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts.","Ignore place value and read digits from left to right as ones only.","Copy the model numbers and call that independent work."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Understand and model\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid.","Writing only the final answer without working does not show the method.","Copy the model numbers and call that independent work.","Treat a missing zero as if it does not change the value."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Show the working\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working.","Changing the answer without repairing the method does not fix the error. Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts.","Treat a missing zero as if it does not change the value.","Skip the working because the first guess looked neat."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Test a misconception\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the method on new numbers or a new context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy and units or places. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use the method on new numbers or a new context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy and units or places.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers.","Skip the working because the first guess looked neat.","Ignore place value and read digits from left to right as ones only."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Transfer to a new problem\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens. Useful feedback uses the original numbers and method.","options":["306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens.","Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"There are 3,060 stickers in packs of 10. How many packs? Show place reasoning.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The most useful working names the quantities and the reason for each step, not only the final answer. Useful feedback uses the original numbers and method.","options":["The most useful working names the quantities and the reason for each step, not only the final answer.","Writing only the final answer without working does not show the method.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Write the key numbers from the model and say what each one represents in the met\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens. Useful feedback uses the original numbers and method.","options":["306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens.","Changing the answer without repairing the method does not fix the error. Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Describe why the warned-against approach gives the wrong value or meaning, then \", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The new problem should use the same method as the model, but contain different numbers. Useful feedback uses the original numbers and method.","options":["The new problem should use the same method as the model, but contain different numbers.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Solve one fresh problem that uses the same skill and write a short reason for yo\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence, not repetition of the worked model, demonstrates the skill.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced relevant working with accurate reasoning and named places or values.","question":"Solve a fresh problem that uses the central skill. Show working and name the places or values that matter.","sample_answer":"Original demonstration: A school has 2,450 pencils. A box holds 100. How many full boxes? 24 full boxes with 50 left over, because 24 hundreds make 2,400.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A correction needs to change value or method, not just make the working longer.","marking_guide":"Require an actual misconception plus corrected working and a method-linked reason.","question":"Name one likely calculation or place-value error, correct it and say why the correction works.","sample_answer":"Common error: Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts. Correction: 306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent working and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-mat-y3-w03-l3","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA mathematics alignment using verified outcome code wording where recorded in lesson-pipeline/sources; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise problem.","Read the mission before you start calculating.","Keep the place or unit you are working with in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your working with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the place or distance that carries the method.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore place value or working.","Prefer accurate method over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your working and reason are both present.","Proofread digits, places and operation signs.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact place, value or distance before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key numbers.","Say what each number represents in the method.","A final answer alone is weaker than labelled working."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with stronger working.","Change the value or method, not only how neat it looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose fresh numbers that still use the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original working and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new numbers."]},"subject":"Number and Algebra","success_criteria":["I can use problem with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify place value and explain why it matters.","I can practise reason independently on a new prompt.","I can notice model needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Place-value problem solving uses digit values and regrouping to answer real questions about quantity, not digit tricks alone. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task.","options":["Place-value problem solving uses digit values and regrouping to answer real questions about quantity, not digit tricks alone.","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no working."],"question":"What should you demonstrate in this teaching stage?"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nA school has 2,450 pencils. A box holds 100. How many full boxes? 24 full boxes with 50 left over, because 24 hundreds make 2,400.\n\nTRY FIRST\nThere are 3,060 stickers in packs of 10. How many packs? Show place reasoning.\n\nFEEDBACK\n306 packs — 3,060 ones = 306 tens.","explain":"Place-value problem solving uses digit values and regrouping to answer real questions about quantity, not digit tricks alone.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Dividing digits separately (3, 0, 6) without place meaning gives nonsense pack counts. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Place-value division into hundreds boxes.","caption":"Use hundreds and leftovers, not digit tricks.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">2,450 pencils</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">boxes of 100</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Full boxes</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">24 with 50 left</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: A school has 2,450 pencils. A box holds 100. How many full boxes? 24 full boxes with 50 l